      "summary": "Kronos: A Foundation Model for the Language of Financial Markets\nPaper: https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.02739v1\nFull article: https://arxiv.org/html/2508.02739v1\n\nKronos models financial candlestick sequences with a discrete tokenizer and an\nautoregressive transformer. Its tokenizer compresses price and trading-activity\ninformation into hierarchical tokens, which the predictor models over time.\nThe paper evaluates forecasting, synthetic sequence generation, and investment\nsimulations, alongside architecture ablations and inference-sampling choices.\n\nNavigation for future work:\n- Section 3: tokenization, hierarchical modeling, pretraining and inference.\n- Section 4: experimental setup, main results and ablations.\n- Appendix B: datasets, cleaning and missing observations.\n- Appendix C: architecture, training and inference configurations.\n- Appendix D: evaluation tasks, baselines, metrics, portfolio rules and costs.\n- Appendices E-F: additional and full experimental results.\n\nMatch the paper version and model checkpoint before comparing results. The local\nfolder provides reduced pretrained inference; consult STATUS.txt and README.md\nfor its actual scope. The original article is the reference for equations,\nnumeric tables, figures and complete protocol details.\n"
    },
